# Documentation Maintenance Protocol:

- Docs are part of the change. A task that modifies behaviour is not done until the matching docs are updated in the same diff.
- Before finishing any task, run the change-to-doc map below, open each mapped file, and update every statement that your change made false. If nothing needs updating, say so explicitly in your final message ("docs checked: <files>, no change needed").
- Never document from memory. Re-read the code you changed and copy names, paths, signatures and commands from it.
- Add a line to `CHANGELOG.md` for user-visible changes, and to `docs/DECISIONS.md` for new dependencies or architectural decisions (one line of justification).
- If a doc and the code disagree, the code wins: fix the doc, and mention it.
- Do not create new top-level docs when an existing file owns the topic.

## Change-to-doc map

Full table: [docs/ai/README.md](docs/ai/README.md#change-to-doc-map).

| If you change... | Update... |
| --- | --- |
| HTTP routes, shapes, auth | `docs/ai/api-reference.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `.cursor/rules/11-api-routes.mdc` |
| CLI / MCP | `docs/ai/api-reference.md`, `README.md`, `integrations/README.md` if listed |
| Graph schema / properties | `docs/ai/data-model.md`, `docs/architecture.md`; bump adapter version |
| Analyzers / parsers | `docs/ai/indexing-pipeline.md`, fixtures, `docs/GAPS.md` |
| Views / algorithms | `docs/ai/architecture-map.md`, `docs/ai/frontend-guide.md`, `docs/graph-architecture-research.md` |
| Frontend UX | `docs/ai/frontend-guide.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/DESIGN.md` |
| Env / data dir | `.env.example`, `docs/ai/runbook.md`, `docs/onboarding.md` |
| Tooling / CI | `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/ai/testing-and-quality.md`, `docs/DECISIONS.md` |
| Security | `docs/SECURITY.md`, `docs/private-repos.md`, `.cursor/rules/40-security-privacy.mdc` |
| Bug (non-obvious) | `CHANGELOG.md`; `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` if agents could repeat it |
| New user-visible feature | `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/GAPS.md` |
